112 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This project focuses on enhancing the quality management practices and software development standards at Saudi Arabian Airlines \(Saudia\), specifically targeting the operational challenges of frequent flight delays. As a key player in the aviation industry, Saudia is committed to providing superior customer experiences and operational efficiency. Frequent flight delays not only undermine passenger satisfaction but also affect the airline's reputation and operational effectiveness.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
113 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The primary objective of this project is to assess and improve Saudia's project management software systems, ensuring they align with international quality standards such as ISO, IATA, and GACA. By examining existing software systems, identifying critical quality measures and performance indicators, and addressing root causes of delays through systematic analysis \(including methodologies like Fishbone Analysis\), this project aims to develop actionable strategies that enhance operational performance.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
114 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Additionally, the project will implement a comprehensive quality framework, fostering a culture of continuous improvement among Saudia's employees. By integrating best practices into the software development lifecycle, the project intends to streamline processes, minimize delays, and elevate service delivery. Ultimately, this project not only positions Saudia as a leader in the aviation sector but also supports the broader goals of the Kingdom's Vision 2030 initiative, emphasizing modernization and excellence in service delivery for the airline industry.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
